--- a/architecture/sandbox.md
+++ b/architecture/sandbox.md
@@ -417,6 +417,31 @@ sandbox workload directly. The relay supports:
 - Tar-based file sync.
 - Port forwarding where supported by the CLI/TUI surface.
 
+Retained-output clients can request typed replay metadata with SSH environment
+request `OPENSHELL_MAIN_EVENTS=1` before attaching `openshell-main`. The value
+is not propagated to the sandbox process. Invalid values and requests after
+attachment fail. Ordinary clients retain raw stdout and stderr without metadata.
+
+The output cursor atomically captures a per-attachment sequence fence. Once it
+has delivered retained events before that fence, it emits one generated
+`openshell.terminal.v1.MainProcessEvent` containing `replay_complete`. The message travels
+on SSH extended-data type `0xFE000001`, in the private-use range defined by
+[RFC 4254 section 5.2](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4254#section-5.2).
+This is an OpenShell adapter extension, not a standardized terminal event.
+The process cannot manufacture metadata by writing escape sequences or stderr.
+The shared log never stores attachment fences. Empty history completes
+immediately; output produced during replay remains after the captured fence.
+Eviction fails the attachment without a completion claim.
+
+Renderers must suppress terminal answerbacks while replaying and drain all
+preceding renderer writes before enabling input or processing live output.
+Neither elapsed time nor an idle stream establishes replay completion. A
+client requiring metadata must fail closed if it never arrives, including
+when an older supervisor acknowledges the generic environment request.
+This event does not grant input ownership, extend authorization, or replace
+the canonical process. Raw stdout/stderr ordering, the output bound, the
+single input lease and disconnect semantics remain unchanged.
+
 Before dropping identity, full-mode canonical and independent PTY children
 transfer their freshly allocated slave descriptor to the same resolved UID/GID
 used for execution, with owner-only mode 0600. They never chown a workload
